From b602afe450fb4d276bf2c385084a3ef98c7aa2bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "DeepSig Inc." <tim.oshea753@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:03:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] connector: native SCTP association link layer (E2AP-style
 framing)

Add E3LinkLayer::SCTP_ASSOCIATION and SctpAssociationE3Connector: one SCTP
one-to-one association per peer carries the setup, inbound and outbound
channels, one E3-PDU per SCTP message (MSG_EOR boundaries, no length
prefix), exactly as E2AP, F1AP and NGAP frame their PDUs. Send/receive
buffers are preset before listen()/connect() and delayed SACK is disabled so
multi-chunk messages do not stall on the kernel's 200 ms SACK timer.

The RAN role serves many peers on one listener: the first message of a fresh
association is routed to the setup channel, later ones are inbound, and
outbound messages are broadcast to every set-up peer (the same semantics as
the ZMQ PUB/SUB and POSIX connectors). The dApp role gates receive() until
the SetupResponse has been consumed by the setup thread.

Tests: tests/test_role_aware_connector_sctp.cpp (connector round trip
including a 200 KiB message) and tests/integration/test_role_pair_sctp.cpp
(E3Agent RAN + dApp pair end to end). Both skip on hosts without SCTP.

Co-authored-by: DeepSig Inc.
